        <div class = "modal-body">
          <p class = "lead">What is PCI</p>
		  <p>The Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS) is a set of standards that businesses must follow in order to protect cardholder data.</p>

<p>It was created by the Payment Card Industry Security Standards Council (PCI SSC), which is a joint effort by Visa, MasterCard, American Express, Discover Financial Services, and JCB.</p>

<p>The PCI DSS covers a wide range of topics, including:</p>

<ul>
    <li>Data security</li>
    <li>Data encryption</li>
    <li>Security policies and procedures</li>
    <li>Employee training</li>
    <li>Security assessments</li>
</ul>

<p>Compliance with the PCI DSS is mandatory for businesses that accept credit and debit cards. Businesses that are not compliant with the PCI DSS may face fines, penalties, and other sanctions.</p>
